Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The encoder and decoder are original implementations written from ISO/IEC
11172-3 (MPEG-1 audio) and ISO/IEC 13818-3 (MPEG-2 audio), the public
descriptions of the MPEG-2.5 extension and of the Xing, LAME and VBRI tags,
and published psychoacoustic literature. They are not translations of, and
do not derive from, any other MPEG audio encoder's or decoder's source; none
was read or run. The normative tables (Huffman codes, scalefactor bands,
the synthesis window, Layer II allocation) are the standards' data;
docs/PROVENANCE.md records each source and how the tables were verified.

The decoder is verified against ISO's own conformance waveforms (ISO/IEC
14496-26), used as data and not distributed here.

